# Build context for Dockerfile.mcp. BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`
# in preference to `.dockerignore`, which is why this file exists rather than a
# shared one: that one excludes parsed-rules-aug-2026.md, because the HTTP image
# has no reader for it, and this image serves it as the rtw://rules resource.
#
# The COPY lines name what they want, so this is defence in depth plus a smaller
# context. The whole web UI goes, which is most of the repository by size --
# nothing reachable from mcp.pl touches it.
.git
.gitignore
.claude
PLANS
README.md
DESIGN.md
prolog/test
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
Dockerfile.mcp.dockerignore
*.log
httpd.log

# The three front ends this image does not serve, and the UI they serve.
prolog/server.pl
prolog/daemon.pl
prolog/cli.pl
prolog/wasm.pl
web

# The UI toolchain and the generators.
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
.impeccable.md
prolog/tools
prolog/data/earn/sources
